      "content": "Yes, seawater density is influenced by both temperature and salinity. Warmer water typically has a lower density, while saltier water tends to have a higher density. In thermohaline circulation, areas of cooler, high-salinity water are denser and can sink, driving a part of ocean currents, while warmer, less salty water tends to stay on the surface, creating stratification. Understanding this interplay helps explain oceanic current patterns and sediment distribution in your AUV data observations.",
